 Throws if `patch` is not a syntactically valid JSON Patch, or if one of its operations fails (for
 example, a `test` operation whose value does not match, or a `remove` of a path that does not exist).
 
+### `applyMergePatch(target, patch)`
+
+Applies a [JSON Merge Patch](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7386) to a JSON document and returns the
+merged document as a new value, leaving `target` unmodified.
+
+```ts
+import { applyMergePatch } from "json-toolkit";
+
+const target = { foo: "bar", baz: { qux: 1 } };
+
+applyMergePatch(target, { baz: { qux: null } }); // { foo: "bar", baz: {} }
+```
+
+A `null` in `patch` removes the corresponding member; an object in `patch` is merged recursively;
+any other value (including an array) replaces the corresponding member wholesale. A non-object
+`patch` replaces `target` entirely.
+
 ## Development
 
 - `npm test` runs the test suite.
